        "The determinism contract requires every side effect, including pi-SDK dispatch, to route through a recorded tool or replay diverges.",
        "Existing runs must be byte-for-byte unchanged, so the new backend defaults off.",
        "Decomposition depth must be dynamic — the task tree has to grow to the problem's contours rather than be fixed by a template."
      ],
      "decision": "Adopt an event-sourced ActiveGraph run as the single source of truth for agent work state, demoting DOT to a compiled read-only projection; fix the work vocabulary as the team_ops containment spine project → milestone → task with action, artifact and evaluation attached as satellites by typed relation; and land Phase A as an additive, default-off event-bus backend that leaves the published JSONL format untouched.",
      "consequences": "Agent work state becomes write-only-as-events: DOT and signal files become projections, never hand-edited sources. Future consumers of the event stream must arrive as `EventEmitter` backends rather than by mutating the JSONL schema. The accepted costs are a young 1.x dependency that must be version-pinned, a projection adapter owed to existing DOT tooling in Phase B, and the engineering work of wrapping every side effect as a recorded tool.",
      "narration": "Three decisions are recorded here, and they nest. The largest says the shared log becomes the authority on what the work is, and the old graph file is demoted to a picture generated from it. The second settles the vocabulary: projects contain milestones, milestones contain tasks, tasks can contain tasks, and everything else — the record of an attempt, the files it produced, the score it earned — hangs off that spine by a named relationship instead of becoming another level in the hierarchy. The third is the narrow one that makes this proposal safe to land now: the first instalment is an extra listener on an existing broadcast, off unless you turn it on, so the format other systems already depend on does not change at all.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "kind": "forces",
          "text": "The change lands under `cobuilder/execution_engine/events/`, which ADR-0008 made a path-gated boundary because ADR-0007 published the events JSONL as a cross-language contract. The gate fires on the path, not on the severity of the change, so an additive backend needs a record naming consumers exactly as a breaking one would."
