        {
          "kind": "forces",
          "text": "Migration cannot break the operators. `tools/pipeline-watch`, `tmux-nav` and `cli.py watch` all read DOT and signal files today, which is why the target state keeps DOT alive as a compiled projection instead of deleting it."
        },
        {
          "kind": "forces",
          "text": "Replay only holds if side effects are recorded. Under activegraph's determinism contract, a pi-SDK dispatch that is not wrapped as a recorded tool makes replay diverge — which is what makes Phase B, not Phase A, the expensive half of this migration."
